  "source": "// Bank \u2014 dynamic Namespace-backed lockbox custody service.\n//\n// Bank is a dynamic CLOOMC LUMP at catalog index 54, not a hardware boot\n// slot. The inner sanctum creates private Outform storage only when needed.\n//\n// Security ABI:\n//   * every public authority is a typed capability register;\n//   * offsets, word counts, kinds, capacities, and status values remain DR\n//     values; and\n//   * the live binding keeps the inner-sanctum passkey private and manages\n//     custody, zeroization, and recovery.\n//\n// The source models lifecycle state only. It cannot manufacture, inspect, or\n// reconstruct authority from integer fields: the CR ABI and proof-bound runtime\n// gate are the sole security boundary for those operations.\n//\n// MintKey is deliberately not a public method. The live Bank binding invokes\n// it only inside the inner sanctum, where it mints or rotates the private\n// passkey and retains its independent proof. No owner key, proof, scalar ID,\n// Namespace address, or reconstructed handle crosses the Bank boundary.\n// Callers use the higher-level methods below with typed Golden Tokens only.\n\nabstraction Bank {\n    capabilities {\n    }\n\n    // Create(lump: CR1 Inform R) -> CR0 = BankVariable Enter capability or NULL,\n    // and DR0 = 1 on success or a Bank error code on failure. CR0 is the\n    // resulting Enter authority; DR0 is diagnostic data and can never authorize\n    // entry. The caller must test CR0 before using the verified abstraction.\n    // The LUMP is checked first: its seals, token, SELF identity, and declared\n    // relationships must agree before the live binding issues this capability.\n    // A hash is an integrity check, not proof of provenance by itself.\n    method Create(lump: capability Inform R) {\n        return(1)\n    }\n\n    // Read and Inspect operate on the typed E capability returned by Create in\n    // CR0. Methods mediate every read of a Bank-owned abstraction; callers\n    // cannot substitute CR3, a raw GT, DR0, or metadata for that capability.\n    // Failed calls preserve the NULL/invalid CR0 state and identify the reason\n    // in DR0 rather than collapsing all failures into one false value.\n    // The binding returns a fresh readable Inform capability in CR4 for Read.\n    // Inspect writes status=DR0, words=DR1, capacity=DR2, issue=DR3, and\n    // lifecycle=DR4; private locations and tokens are never materialised.\n    method Read(variable: capability BankVariable E, offset, words) {\n        if (offset < 0) {\n            return(0)\n        }\n        if (words <= 0) {\n            return(0)\n        }\n        return(1)\n    }\n\n    method InspectVariable(variable: capability BankVariable E) {\n        return(1)\n    }\n\n    // Release and RevokeVariable retire the verified variable, zeroize its\n    // private storage, and clear CR0. A BankVariable capability (CR0) is the\n    // only public authority for the verified variable it names. The binding\n    // resolves that typed Golden Token to private custody state and retains\n    // the passkey/proof internally; callers never receive the private record.\n    // Nested variables are created by calling Create on a readable result from\n    // Read, never by exposing inner-sanctum state.\n    method Release(variable: capability BankVariable E) {\n        return(1)\n    }\n\n    method RevokeVariable(variable: capability BankVariable E) {\n        return(1)\n    }\n\n}",
